 "intervention": "asm-preprocessing rewrite of `cror eq,[crN]{gt|lt},[crN]eq ; bne|beq T` into the equivalent strict/inclusive branch on the same bit: gt+bne->blt, gt+beq->bge, lt+bne->bgt, lt+beq->ble (crN operand kept). The cror becomes a nop. Exact for every total-order compare (integer cmp, and fcmp on ordered operands). Residual difference: float UNORDERED (NaN) sets only the UN bit, so the original takes the `bne` and the rewrite does not; C has no UN, m2c already ignores it. Not applied when cr0.eq is read again on the fall-through path or the branch is not the very next instruction.",
